**Quick‑start fishing script**

```ts
// /tmp/fish_loop.ts
import { bot, sdk } from "rs-agent";

async function main() {
  // 1️⃣  Skip the tutorial (only needed the first time)
  await bot.skipTutorial();

  // 2️⃣  Find the nearest fishing spot and keep fishing
  while (true) {
    // Locate a fishing spot (the spot is a “loc” object)
    const spot = await sdk.findNearbyLoc(/Fishing Spot/i);
    if (!spot) {
      console.log("⚠️  No fishing spot nearby – wandering a bit");
      // Walk a little in case we’re standing on a bad tile
      await bot.walkTo(
        sdk.getState().player.worldX + 1,
        sdk.getState().player.worldZ
      );
      continue;
    }

    // Grab a net from inventory (the default starter provides a “Small fishing net”)
    const net = await sdk.findInventoryItem(/small fishing net/i);
    if (!net) {
      console.error("❌  No net in inventory – can’t fish");
      break;
    }

    // 3️⃣  Fish!  The “Fish” option works on most spots, but “Lure” gives a higher XP rate.
    const result = await bot.useItemOnLoc(net, spot);   // net → spot
    if (result?.error) {
      console.error("⚡  Interaction failed:", result.error);
      // If the spot is out of range, walk a step toward it and retry
      await bot.walkTo(spot.worldX, spot.worldZ);
    } else {
      // Successful catch – the bot automatically eats/shows the caught fish.
      console.log("🐟  Caught a fish!");
    }

    // 4️⃣  Small pause to avoid spamming the server (the game’s own tick‑rate already throttles actions,
    //    but a tiny delay prevents “Too many actions” dialogs)
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 200));
  }
}

// Run the loop immediately
main().catch(e => console.error("❗  Unhandled error:", e));
```

**How to run**

```bash
# 1. Make sure you have the “agent” bot set up (credentials in bots/agent/bot.env)
# 2. Start the script in the background – it will keep fishing for as long as you let it run.
bun /tmp/fish_loop.ts > /tmp/fish.log 2>&1 &
```

**Checking progress**

Every 15 seconds the benchmark harness records raw XP. To see your *real‑game* XP‑rate (the score you need),

```bash
