**Script – `/tmp/train_magic.ts`**

```ts
// Run with: bun /tmp/train_magic.ts > /tmp/train_magic.log 2>&1 &
(async () => {
  // 1️⃣  Leave tutorial island
  await bot.skipTutorial();

  // 2️⃣  Train Magic for 30 min
  const endTime = Date.now() + 30 * 60 * 1000; // 30 minutes

  while (Date.now() < endTime) {
    // Find a chicken (or any low‑level NPC)
    const npc = sdk.findNearbyNpc(/chicken/i);
    if (!npc) {
      // If none is nearby, wander a bit then retry
      await bot.walkTo(sdk.getState().player.worldX + 1, sdk.getState().player.worldZ);
      continue;
    }

    // Cast the first spell component (usually "Wind Strike")
    // Adjust the number if a different component is needed.
    const result = await bot.castSpellOnNpc(npc, 1);
    // Ignore failures – they are harmless; the loop will keep trying.
  }

  // Optional: report finish
  console.log('Magic training complete');
})();
```

**Why this works**

* `bot.castSpellOnNpc` is the high‑level method that sends the spell‑cast packet and waits for the action to finish.  
* Using a low‑level NPC (chicken) keeps the combat quick, maximizing XP per real‑time minute.  
* The loop runs continuously for the full 30 minutes; the benchmark’s 15‑second sampling will capture the peak XP rate automatically.  

